      "message": "Consider keeping `av1/common/reconintra.h` free of `\u003cemmintrin.h\u003e` and `#if defined(__SSE2__)` (lines 221-270 in `av1_fill_block_lbd`): every other `\u003cemmintrin.h\u003e` include in libaom lives under `*/x86/*`, and gating on compiler-predefined `__SSE2__` / `_M_X64` rather than `HAVE_SSE2` / RTCD causes `-DAOM_TARGET_CPU\u003dgeneric` / `-DENABLE_SSE2\u003d0` builds on x86-64 to still emit SSE2 intrinsics in `reconintra.c`, and makes both `av1_predict_dc_block_lbd_c` and `av1_predict_dc_block_lbd_sse2` execute the same `#if defined(__SSE2__)` branch in `LowbdPredictDcBlockTest.Sse2MatchesC` (leaving the `#else` `memset` loop untested on x86 CI). Moving the `_mm_storeu_si128` fill helper into `av1/common/x86/reconintra_sse2.c` and keeping `av1_fill_block_lbd` pure C (`memset(dst, val, 16/32/64)` per row, which compilers already lower to unaligned vector stores) avoids both issues.",
